Fix badly-cropped hero/banner photos on Sponsor and Impact pages (v0.3.2)

The Sponsor and Impact page banners used a fixed-height, full-width box
with background-position: center (or an under-tuned, uncommitted
override) against source photos where the child's face sat well above
center. At common desktop widths this cropped the face out entirely,
leaving only a neck/collar on Sponsor and a doctor's coat on Impact -
reported directly as hero/header images being "so much cropped."

Measured each source image's actual face position with a pixel grid,
then derived and empirically verified (at 400/768/1280/1920px) a
background-position offset that keeps the face in frame at every width:
sponsor.html/sw to "center 27%", impact.html/sw to "center 30%". Checked
every other banner and the home hero the same way; no other page showed
the defect.

Also documents, in OPEN_ITEMS.md, two things intentionally left
unchanged: About and Blog still have no banner photo, and Blog has no
imagery at all - both flagged in a design review, neither fixed here
since closing them needs either new photography or a judgment call on
reusing existing photos.

Re-ran the 146-check bilingual Playwright suite: no regressions.
Bumped version to 0.3.2 and restamped all pages.

